          "secNumber": "5.2",
          "heading": "Geophysical foundation and the measurement-to-model chain",
          "content": "The measured total magnetic field combines core field, time-dependent external contributions and crustal magnetization. Rock response includes induced magnetization proportional to susceptibility and, in many rocks, remanent magnetization that can dominate or oppose the induced component. Reduction to pole, continuation and derivative transformations depend on assumptions and can amplify noise. Diurnal basestation corrections and position control are necessary before geological interpretation. Polarity patterns support tectonic reconstructions only when the relevant age and magnetization history is independently justified. The reference model removes a major-scale field, not all environmental interference or crustal complexity.",
